<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its picture (architect 2026-10-12; the metronome since
     2026-10-16): the architect's digital metronome, the caption's icon and
     the glyph Warp wears, assets/icons/adwaita-3.22/AppIcon.svg, rasterised
     ANTIALIASED by rsvg-convert (librsvg on the laptop; a vector, not pixel
     art) and centered over THE CHROME'S OWN CAPTION START, FLAT (architect
     2026-10-16: "just the title start color, flat, as the bg"): Windows
     Storm's active title start #800080 (chrome_schemes.inc's windows-storm
     row, the compiled scheme), one color over the whole canvas, so the mask
     shows a purple shape carrying the drawing (the Cool Edit case's 20
     face-ramp bands under Midnight's Face from 2026-10-12 until then). An
     ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so
     no legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/, BOTH written by
     tools/app_icon/gen_app_icon.sh (which also writes the Linux desktop icon,
     packaging/warptempo_gui.svg, the same drawing bare):
       ic_launcher_background.png  the full 108 dp canvas flat in #800080;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the drawing rendered at the 64 dp art size,
                                   centred on a transparent canvas of the
                                   density's full 108 dp.

     THE 66 dp SAFE ZONE: an adaptive foreground's art must sit inside the
     mask's guaranteed-visible inner zone, Android's own 66 dp of the 108 dp
     canvas. The 48-unit drawing at 64 dp square (4/3 dp a unit) sits just
     inside that zone, the same 64 dp at every density (the per-density PNG
     pixel size scales with the density factor f alone):

       density  f    canvas C=108f  art 64f  offset (C-64f)/2
       mdpi     1    108            64       22
       hdpi     1.5  162            96       33
       xhdpi    2    216            128      44
       xxhdpi   3    324            192      66
       xxxhdpi  4    432            256      88

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop
     and committed; a change of the drawing or the ground is a re-run of the generator
     (bash tools/app_icon/gen_app_icon.sh, byte-stable), never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
